<p>U.S. forces were still searching on April 4 for a missing crew member from an F-15E Strike Eagle shot down over Iran, after rescuing the other crew member in what multiple outlets described as the first known U.S. fighter aircraft brought down by hostile fire inside Iran since the war began nearly five weeks ago. Several reports also said a second U.S. aircraft, described in many accounts as an A-10, was hit near the Strait of Hormuz or elsewhere in the Gulf region, and its pilot was rescued. The incident marks a clear escalation in a conflict that sources say began after U.S. and Israeli attacks on Tehran on February 28. It has also raised the stakes because Iran and the United States are now racing to find the missing airman. President Trump said the F-15 loss would not affect negotiations with Iran, while U.S. officials pointed to the ongoing rescue effort and Iranian state media said local authorities were offering rewards for help finding the missing American crew member.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/VeKQNpsyNJRdsATCB9Z_67uZ-3jgnmuj5ke7C2YI6WFz-FQidOOF5OpQbtV1b7p1kgmWZ4Hud-mxpfct_gfFDdVJVzlF6As0v2P03_e1soPE' alt='Iranian state media image said to show fragments of a downed U.S. jet in central Iran on April 3, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Helicopters under fire: Two Black Hawk helicopters involved in the rescue mission took Iranian fire but made it out of Iranian airspace, though it remained unclear whether their crews were injured.</li><li>Ground rescue risk: Some outlets said U.S. special forces entered Iran to recover one F-15E crew member, a sign Washington was willing to push beyond an air-only rescue.</li><li>Claims of sky control tested: The downings undercut recent assertions by President Trump and Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth that U.S. forces had established control of Iranian skies.</li><li>Second jet details remain murky: While many reports said the second aircraft was lost near the Strait of Hormuz, Reuters via Dawn said the A-10 crashed in Kuwait after taking Iranian fire, highlighting how much about that episode remains uncertain.</li></ul><blockquote>No, not at all. No, it’s war. We’re in war. - President Donald Trump</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>President Trump: Before the downing, Trump said the military campaign could end in two to three weeks, a timeline the aircraft losses now seem to complicate. (<a href='https://www.politico.com/news/2026/04/03/us-military-launches-rescue-mission-for-pilots-who-crashed-in-iran-00857479'>Politico</a>)</li><li>Iranian military: Iran’s military said it used a &#x27;new advanced defence system&#x27; to shoot down the F-15 and also claimed it brought down another U.S. aircraft south of Qeshm Island. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1988290/irans-military-claims-shooting-down-second-us-jet-while-hunt-for-crew-of-downed-f-15-aircraft-continues'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Iran’s Revolutionary Guard Corps: The IRGC said it was combing the area for the missing U.S. crew member, underscoring that Tehran saw the search as an active military objective. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1988487/iran-us-race-to-find-crew-member-of-crashed-american-fighter-jet'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Analyst Firas Maksad: Firas Maksad said the prospect of a captured U.S. crew member could push President Trump to intensify the military campaign rather than scale it back. (<a href='https://www.politico.com/news/2026/04/03/us-military-launches-rescue-mission-for-pilots-who-crashed-in-iran-00857479'>Politico</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/f-15-fighter-jet-a-10-warthog-fighter-aircraft-black-hawk-helicopters-us-planes-hit-over-iran-2-pilots-rescued-1-missing-donald-trump-briefed-11309099#publisher=newsstand'>2 US Fighter Jets, Black Hawk Choppers Hit By Iran, 2 Pilots Rescued, 1 Missing</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/iran-war-search-on-for-missing-crew-member-of-downed-us-jet/live-76657680'>Iran war: S